    "other-towing-roadside-duplicate@01": {
      "ask": "Ask each plan what it covers and what it costs, starting with your car insurer if you have a roadside add-on there. If another plan already gives you the same help, ask your agent to take the add-on off your car policy.",
      "background": "Towing or roadside coverage on a car insurance policy pays for things like a tow when your car is disabled. The National Association of Insurance Commissioners (NAIC, a group of state insurance regulators) calls it an optional extra, separate from the basic policy, and says an auto club such as AAA or another membership may already include some of the same help. You told us you get roadside help from a roadside add-on on your car insurance, an auto club membership and roadside help that came with your car, so you may be paying for the same tow more than once. Plans differ, so ask each one what it covers.",
      "bucket": "drop",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reason": "I already get roadside help from another plan, so I want to know whether I need to keep paying for this one.",
      "sources": [
        "naic-what-does-auto-insurance-cover",
        "naic-consumer-insight-right-protection",
        "naic-shopping-tool-auto-2023"
      ],
      "title": "Check whether you are paying twice for roadside help"
    },
