      "background": "Your home policy's liability limit is the most it pays if someone is hurt on your property or you are held responsible for harm to someone else. An umbrella is extra liability coverage that starts paying only after that limit is used up, and umbrella insurers set a minimum for what has to be underneath. You told us yours asks for $300,000 and your home policy has a limit lower than $300,000. For a $1 million umbrella, the Insurance Information Institute says most insurers want about $300,000 of home liability, and yours is lower than that. We found no published rule for what happens when the limit underneath is below that minimum, so the safe move is to close the gap rather than find out during a claim.",
