      "background": "The Insurance Information Institute describes the usual underlying limits as what most insurers want, so your umbrella insurer may ask for something different, and not being sure of yours is fine. You were not sure about your auto liability limit, your home liability limit, your motorcycle liability limit and your boat liability limit, and about what your umbrella asks for on your auto, home, motorcycle and boat policies, so we cannot tell whether your limits meet what your umbrella asks for. An umbrella is extra liability coverage that starts paying only after the limits underneath are used up.",
